    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d403">

                <pb facs="0449" n="365" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp02/pg365"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. No. 814.01B</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Minister in Guatemala</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Leavell</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-06-26T16:00:00-04:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 26, 1918, 4 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your June 24, 11 a.m. Yes. If Government of Guatemala has decided to appoint such
                    an official, Department would see no objection to
                    Hodgsdon.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
